<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Cartesian transformation of the human skull into chimpanzee, baboon and dog (Figs. 404-408) (Homo sapiens, Pan troglodytes, Papio ursinus, Canis lupus familiaris (lateral skull))",
        "Thompson (1917) Cartesian transformation of the human skull into chimpanzee, baboon and dog (Figs. 404-408) faithfully reproduces Homo sapiens, Pan troglodytes, Papio ursinus, Canis lupus familiaris (lateral skull) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-058-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-058-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-058-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-058-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) thompson/claims/t1917-058_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Homo sapiens, Pan troglodytes, Papio ursinus, Canis lupus familiaris (lateral skull) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-058_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py> ;
    schema:about "Homo sapiens, Pan troglodytes, Papio ursinus, Canis lupus familiaris (lateral skull)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Nothing about growth, ontogeny or phylogeny; no claim that Thompson's particular curves are the optimal smooth map; the 'supported' verdict of v1 carries no confidence interval (remediation R1).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: The Fig. 405 net digitised (skeleton junctions + 4 manual corners), reconstructed as a thin-plate spline T in human grid units (E1-E3); cell-area log-linear regression (E4); 11 homologous landmarks digitised by the loop agent on Fig. 404, Fig. 406 and four Commons specimens; full-Procrustes explained fraction of T(H) toward the real chimpanzee (E6); displacement-field cosines and intensity ratios between real specimens; facial index and Camper-type facial angle (E7).",
        "reported_in_source: Thompson (1917) pp. 770-773: the human skull drawn in a 5x4 Cartesian net (Fig. 404) and the chimpanzee, baboon and dog skulls drawn in deformed nets (Figs. 405-408); prose statements that the deformation is one 'harmonious and congruent transformation', that cell areas increase 'in approximately logarithmic order' from above downwards and behind forwards, that the baboon differs 'only in an increased intensity', that the chimpanzee is 'much nearer the human type than the baboon', and that the dog's net 'tapers away in front' on 'different lines'.",
        "transfer_boundary: One specimen per taxon (museum photographs for chimpanzee, baboon, dog; a rendered anatomical model for the human); the baboon and dog nets of Figs. 407-408 were not digitised, so sub-claims C2/C5 are tested on real specimens only, not on Thompson's drawings of them." ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-058_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py; output: docs/media/t1917_058_on_the_theory_of_transformatio_comparison.png; organism: Homo sapiens, Pan troglodytes, Papio ursinus, Canis lupus familiaris (lateral skull); environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Thompson (1917) pp. 770-773: the human skull drawn in a 5x4 Cartesian net (Fig. 404) and the chimpanzee, baboon and dog skulls drawn in deformed nets (Figs. 405-408); prose statements that the deformation is one 'harmonious and congruent transformation', that cell areas increase 'in approximately logarithmic order' from above downwards and behind forwards, that the baboon differs 'only in an increased intensity', that the chimpanzee is 'much nearer the human type than the baboon', and that the dog's net 'tapers away in front' on 'different lines'.; reconstructed_in_script: The Fig. 405 net digitised (skeleton junctions + 4 manual corners), reconstructed as a thin-plate spline T in human grid units (E1-E3); cell-area log-linear regression (E4); 11 homologous landmarks digitised by the loop agent on Fig. 404, Fig. 406 and four Commons specimens; full-Procrustes explained fraction of T(H) toward the real chimpanzee (E6); displacement-field cosines and intensity ratios between real specimens; facial index and Camper-type facial angle (E7).; transfer_boundary: One specimen per taxon (museum photographs for chimpanzee, baboon, dog; a rendered anatomical model for the human); the baboon and dog nets of Figs. 407-408 were not digitised, so sub-claims C2/C5 are tested on real specimens only, not on Thompson's drawings of them.; does_not_claim: Nothing about growth, ontogeny or phylogeny; no claim that Thompson's particular curves are the optimal smooth map; the 'supported' verdict of v1 carries no confidence interval (remediation R1).]; other sources: On Growth and Form, Ch. XVII On the Theory of Transformations, pp. 770-773, Figs. 404-408 <https://archive.org/details/ongrowthform1917thom>; phenomenon_size: 1.3 cm (0.01254 m, log10=-1.902 m, tier=7_organism_cm); species_scale_ladder (1 runs from 1.3 cm to 1.3 cm): 1.3 cm:epithelioid-cyst-buckling" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1109/34.24792>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1525-142X.2005.05027.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.7r85116> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-058-on-the-theory-of-transformatio-audit-thompson1917-t1917-058-1>,
