<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Cartesian transformation of the human skull into chimpanzee, baboon and dog (Figs. 404-408) — Code-to-model traceability: 75/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring maps E1-E7 and the Lean laws to functions and to Thompson's page/figure numbers; each sub-claim C1-C6 cites the sentence of pp. 770-773 it operationalises (scout manifest). Deduction: the correspondence between the digitised Fig. 405 nodes and the figure's labels is documented in the reference JSON but not re-derived or checked by code." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5.1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Cartesian transformation of the human skull into chimpanzee, baboon and dog (Figs. 404-408) — Model fidelity to source: 70/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Thompson's method is implemented as published - a Cartesian net of the human skull and its smooth deformation - using the standard modern formalisation (Bookstein 1989 TPS: exact interpolation of the drawn nodes, affine + bending decomposition), and the net itself is Thompson's own Fig. 405 rather than a re-drawn analogue. Four Lean 4 laws (affine cell congruence, log-area gradient, intensity family, rectangular-vs-triangular taper) are kernel-checked, 0 sorry. Deductions: the baboon and dog nets (Figs. 407-408) are not digitised, so Thompson's own drawn transformations for those taxa are not reconstructed; the TPS regularisation lambda and intensity k are CLI options but never swept in v1." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5.1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-058/scout_manifest.json L1–L40: Fig. 407/408 nets not extractable by the automatic method - baboon/dog tested on real specimens only <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/6475519d7/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-058/scout_manifest.json#L1-L40>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 7e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Cartesian transformation of the human skull into chimpanzee, baboon and dog (Figs. 404-408) — Morphometric validation: 50/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Scale-free morphometrics (Procrustes distances, explained fraction, displacement cosines, cell-area log gradient, facial index, facial angle) are computed on the real specimens and the facial angles (89/68/56/45 deg) fall in the textbook Camper bands for man / chimpanzee / baboon / dog. Deductions: no confidence intervals or permutation null for the 35 % headline; no goodness-of-fit statistics (r, RMSE, KS) beyond R^2 of the area fit; no literature landmark table was found to compare against; the C5 'different lines' test (cos chimp-dog 0.78 vs chimp-baboon 0.78) is a tie and not a meaningful discriminator." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5.1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-058_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py L450–L480: verdict_from: 11 point-estimate binary checks, no uncertainty <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/6475519d7/thompson/claims/t1917-058_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py#L450-L480>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-measurement-affine-fraction-of-the-human-baboon-landmark-displacement-e2-e3-decomposition>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-measurement-affine-fraction-of-the-human-chimpanzee-landmark-displacement-e2-e3-decomposition>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-measurement-affine-fraction-of-the-human-dog-landmark-displacement-e2-e3-decomposition>,
