<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Cartesian transformation of the human skull into chimpanzee, baboon and dog (Figs. 404-408) — Morphological realism / specimen match: 55/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Rendered side by side (panel c vs Fig. 406) the human drawing warped through the digitised net is recognisably Thompson's chimpanzee figure, and the quantitative test against a REAL chimpanzee specimen is positive (35 % explained, T(H) closer to the real chimp than to the real human). Deductions: n = 1 specimen per taxon; the human 'specimen' is a rendered anatomical model, not a museum photograph; all landmarks were digitised by the loop agent (+/- ~12 px) with no uncertainty propagated; the human drawing itself sits d_P = 0.21 from the human specimen, two-thirds of the human-chimp distance, so drawing fidelity is a confound." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5.1> ;
